  "pli-tv-kd4:1.14.15": "",
  "pli-tv-kd4:1.14.16": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Navakena bhikkhunā</i> could be rendered “a/the junior monk”. Yet the point here is that only the most senior member of the Sangha should use the semi-informal address <i lang='pi' translate='no'>āvuso</i>, whereas everyone else should use the formal equivalent <i lang='pi' translate='no'>bhante</i>. In this context, then, <i lang='pi' translate='no'>navaka</i> does not have its normal meaning of “newly ordained” monk, but rather refers to any monk junior to the most senior one. ",
