  "pli-tv-kd4:16.16.1": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Ce</i>, “if”, does not fit in the current context, since there is no main clause corresponding to the conditional clause. Perhaps this is an ancient mistake, whereby the <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ce</i> has been added on the pattern of the similar phrases above. I translate as if the <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ce</i> is not there. ",
  "pli-tv-kd4:16.16.2": "",
  "pli-tv-kd4:16.16.3": "",
  "pli-tv-kd4:16.16.4": "Vin-vn-ṭ 2777: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sānuvādoti ettha anuvādo nāma codanā, saha anuvādena vattatīti sānuvādo</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sānuvādo</i>: here accusing is called <i lang='pi' translate='no'>anuvādo</i>. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Sānuvādo</i> means he proceeds with an accusation.” ",
